## Notices from the car''s Tracker (release 48)

Every car has a Tracker, as your rental agreement says (section 12). If it records something, we tell you at once by email, text or the app: what happened, any charge, and the clause of your agreement.

- **Speeding over 180, 220 or 300 km/h**: one speeding charge an event, at the highest limit reached ($500, $1,000 or $2,500 plus HST). It is taken from your deposit first.
- A speed well over the limit, or hard braking: a friendly heads-up. No charge.
- **The car outside Ontario, past its return time, or its Tracker unplugged**: please call us.
- **The car at an impound lot**: call us at once so we can get it released. The towing and storage costs are yours.

1. Open the notice, or your booking page.
2. Call us if something is wrong or you have a question. We would rather sort it out with you.

> Note: You can turn the heads-up messages off under **Notifications**. Notices about a charge are always sent.
