the place</b>.</li><li>We also tell you by email, text or the app when one happens.</li></ul><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> and the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing there? It says nothing was recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To stop these alerts or change how they reach you, open <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b> and turn <b class="gd-ui">Tracker alert on your car</b> off or on.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Note</span><div>There is nothing for you to do. CarmaCars handles each one with the renter and collects any charge with its evidence. You see the event and the place only, never the renter or the booking.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-the-onboarding-checklist" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The onboarding checklist</h2><p class="gd-p">Home and each car&#39;s page show the same <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding checklist</b>. Each step says one of four things: done, to do (and who it waits on: you, CarmaCars, or another office such as the registry), blocked (and why, for example &quot;First: terms approved&quot;), or not needed. A step that waits on you has one button: the one thing to do for it, such as <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Upload the ownership permit</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-change-an-onboarding-photo" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change an onboarding photo</h2><p class="gd-p">A wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender&#39;s letter? Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Your onboarding photos</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> and choose the new photo or PDF. The new one is checked again by CarmaCars, even if the old one was approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove the photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every change is kept in our history. CarmaCars staff can replace or remove a photo for you too.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-add-several-cars-at-once" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add several cars at once</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add cars from a VIN list</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Paste the VINs (one a line), or upload a CSV or text file. Up to 50 at a time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b>: each VIN is read (year, make and model). A typo (the check digit does not match), a car already with us or one listed twice is shown and not added.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Say for each car whether it is owned outright, financed or leased (with the lender), then press <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Each car then waits for us to approve its terms, like any new car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-service-and-maintenance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Service and maintenance</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, under Service and maintenance.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>What is due on your car (oil change, tires, brakes, inspections, the registration) and the tires on it.</li><li>Every service we recorded: the date, the odometer, the shop, what was done and who paid.</li><li>You pay for maintenance and routine wear (your agreement, 11.1). A service we paid for shows its amount and is deducted on your next statement as an owner cost.</li><li>It is read only: call or message us about a service.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-take-new-listing-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Take new listing photos</h2><p class="gd-p">Good photos get more bookings. You can shoot them yourself with your phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the car&#39;s page, press <b class="gd-ui">Add listing photos</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Take new photos</b> for a car already live).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read the tips for each shot: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take photo</b> for each shot in the list. Press <b class="gd-ui">Retake</b> if one is not right.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The bar shows how many required photos you have.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Submit for listing</b>. New photos replace the current ones once our team approves them.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/610"><img src="/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-d0b13740.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="610"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.3%;top:43.4%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.9%;top:70.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-price-limits" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Price limits</h2><p class="gd-p">Choose the lowest and the highest daily rate your cars are rented at.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Price limits for every car</b>, at the bottom: type a <b class="gd-ui">Minimum a day</b> and a <b class="gd-ui">Maximum a day</b> in dollars, or leave one empty for no limit. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save price limits</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">One car different? Open it: <b class="gd-ui">Price limits</b> has the same two fields for that car only. Empty there, your limits for every car apply.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Short-notice and booked-ahead pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers keep the rental a day between them; fees, add-ons and tax are not counted. Only a CarmaCars Admin can make an exception on one booking, and it is recorded.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-pickup-and-return-records-cars-you-referred-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pickup and return records, cars you referred (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner and return to owner</b> shows the car&#39;s condition when we picked it up from you and when we gave it back: the photos, km and fuel. If you referred another owner, <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Cars you referred</b> shows their cars&#39; bookings, use and revenue, read only, and your referral share is a line on your statements.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-studio-photos-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Studio photos (release 48)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>We make studio photos of your car from its own photos, so every car on CarmaCars looks photographed the same way. The side profile is first.</li><li>Your own photos stay on the page, right after the studio photos. The page tells renters which ones are studio photos.</li><li>We email you when they are live. If the colour or wheels look wrong, reply and we make them again. You can turn this email off in <b class="gd-ui">Account</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b>.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'bookings-and-your-own-use', 'chapter', 'home-and-your-vehicles', 'See every booking in your cars on a calendar, and book a car for yourself when it is free.

## See your bookings

1. Cars > Bookings shows two months of your cars on a calendar. Each block is a booking number.
2. All bookings lists every trip with its car, dates, amount and status.

![](/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-be31cbae.jpg "desktop; size: 980 1092; address: carmacars.ca/owner/bookings; pins: 1 53.1 15.8, 2 12.2 94.5")

> Good to know: A booking can show as Booked, with its dates and no amount: its amounts show once we approve the statement that covers it, and your statement carries every booking you can see, and every booking paid by the renter. The only bookings left out are an insurance replacement we hide from you and an insurer-billed rental that does not block your car''s calendar: they are not part of your revenue, so they stay off your statements and payouts, and you see only that the car is unavailable for those dates. If one of them later starts counting, you get the new booking email then. Unavailable is time your car is in use by us with no revenue for you (for example an insurance hold). A booking expense or a Revenue Share set for one booking is listed on that booking with the reason, and on your statement.

## Rental history

Cars > Bookings also has the **Rental history**: every rental on your cars.

1. Each line: the booking number, the car and its plate, the pickup and the return, the days, the status and your earnings from your approved statements. Not on an approved statement yet: it says so.
2. Choose one car or all, and oldest or newest first. The totals at the top count every rental in the list.
3. Renter details, payments and deposits are never shown, and a cancelled booking is listed only when a charge was kept.

## Book your own car

You pay no rental charge, fee or deposit. A renter''s confirmed booking comes first. Any car still in the program can be booked, a car still onboarding too; if one cannot be booked on your dates (out of service, or a renter has it), the form says why.

1. Open Cars > Bookings and use **Book my own car** on the right (or **Book it for myself** on the car''s page).
2. Choose the Vehicle, then the Pickup and Return date and time.
3. Who''s driving? Choose Me, or Someone else for a family member or friend: add their full name, email, phone and date of birth. They are the main driver: they get their own link to add their licence and a selfie and to sign the rental agreement (the main driver needs an Ontario licence). You sign too.
4. Add a Note (optional) for our team.
5. Tick that you are responsible for the booking: the deductible ($2,500) and any damage, tickets, tolls and fees during it are billed to you, whoever drives, each with its evidence.
6. Press **Book my car**.

![](/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-a4500851.jpg "desktop; size: 450 570; address: carmacars.ca/owner/bookings; pins: 2 92.2 14.6, 3 92.2 64.9, 4 42.2 89.6")

> Good to know: An owner booking earns no revenue and is not on your statement. No price and no deposit apply to you. One booking can be 30 days at most, and you sign the rental agreement before pickup.

## Rideshare and repeat renters (release 35)

Renters may drive for rideshare and delivery platforms with the documents we issue. Verified repeat renters can book your car instantly when it is free, within your price limits.', 'Bookings and your own use', 'The bookings calendar and booking your own car.',
  'See every booking in your cars on a calendar, and book a car for yourself when it is free.

## See your bookings

Cars > Bookings is in this order (release 48):

1. **Your cars, the next six weeks**: a row for each car and a bar for each booking, with today as a red line. A green bar is a trip under way, black is booked, grey is finished, an outlined bar is your own use and a hatched bar is time your car is unavailable. A car with nothing booked says Free these weeks.
2. More than one car? Press a car''s name under the timeline to see only that car, or **All cars**.
3. Three lists, with how many bookings each holds: **On a trip** (out with a renter now), **Upcoming** (booked ahead, the next pickup first) and **Past** (finished and cancelled, the newest first). The page opens on the first one that has a booking.
4. Each booking is one card: its dates, the car, the booking number, its status, and its money on the right. The money is the rental charge before tax when you can see it; **Booked** means the amount comes with your approved statement; **Unavailable** is not part of your revenue; **Your booking** is your own use at no charge. A booking expense or a Revenue Share set for one booking is listed on its card.
5. The line above each list adds it up: the bookings, the rental days, the rental charges shown, and how many amounts are still to come with a statement. Your share and every deduction are on your statement.
6. **Calendar: this month and next**, at the bottom, shows the same bookings on a month calendar.

![](/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-be31cbae.jpg "desktop; size: 980 1092; address: carmacars.ca/owner/bookings; pins: 1 53.1 15.8, 2 12.2 94.5")

