ds it up: the bookings, the rental days, the rental charges shown, and how many amounts are still to come with a statement. Your share and every deduction are on your statement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Calendar: this month and next</b>, at the bottom, shows the same bookings on a month calendar.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/bookings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:980/1092"><img src="/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-be31cbae.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="980" height="1092"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.1%;top:15.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:12.2%;top:94.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A booking can show as Booked, with its dates and no amount: its amounts show once we approve the statement that covers it, and your statement carries every booking you can see, and every booking paid by the renter. The only bookings left out are an insurance replacement we hide from you and an insurer-billed rental that does not block your car&#39;s calendar: they are not part of your revenue, so they stay off your statements and payouts, and you see only that the car is unavailable for those dates. If one of them later starts counting, you get the new booking email then. Unavailable is time your car is in use by us with no revenue for you (for example an insurance hold). A booking expense or a Revenue Share set for one booking is listed on that booking with the reason, and on your statement.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="bookings-and-your-own-use-rental-history" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rental history</h2><p class="gd-p">Cars &gt; Bookings also has the <b class="gd-ui">Rental history</b>: every rental on your cars.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each line: the booking number, the car and its plate, the pickup and the return, the days, the status and your earnings from your approved statements. Not on an approved statement yet: it says so.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose one car or all, and oldest or newest first. The totals at the top count every rental in the list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Renter details, payments and deposits are never shown, and a cancelled booking is listed only when a charge was kept.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="bookings-and-your-own-use-book-your-own-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book your own car</h2><p class="gd-p">You pay no rental charge, fee or deposit. A renter&#39;s confirmed booking comes first. Any car still in the program can be booked, a car still onboarding too; if one cannot be booked on your dates (out of service, or a renter has it), the form says why.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Cars &gt; Bookings and use <b class="gd-ui">Book my own car</b> on the right (or <b class="gd-ui">Book it for myself</b> on the car&#39;s page).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the Vehicle, then the Pickup and Return date and time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Who&#39;s driving? Choose Me, or Someone else for a family member or friend: add their full name, email, phone and date of birth. They are the main driver: they get their own link to add their licence and a selfie and to sign the rental agreement (the main driver needs an Ontario licence). You sign too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add a Note (optional) for our team.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Tick that you are responsible for the booking: the deductible ($2,500) and any damage, tickets, tolls and fees during it are billed to you, whoever drives, each with its evidence.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Book my car</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/bookings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:450/570"><img src="/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-a4500851.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="450" height="570"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.2%;top:14.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.2%;top:64.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.2%;top:89.6%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>An owner booking earns no revenue and is not on your statement. No price and no deposit apply to you. One booking can be 30 days at most, and you sign the rental agreement before pickup.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="bookings-and-your-own-use-rideshare-and-repeat-renters-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rideshare and repeat renters (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters may drive for rideshare and delivery platforms with the documents we issue. Verified repeat renters can book your car instantly when it is free, within your price limits.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'quick-reference', 'reference', 'notices-profile-and-leaving', '### Where things are

| Item | What it is for |
| --- | --- |
| **Home** | The next thing to do first, then what you earned this month, cars out, the next payout and fees due, your cars and what is coming up |
| **Cars** | **Your cars** (each car: terms, checklist, uploads, photos, Leaving) and **Bookings** (all bookings, the calendar, Book my own car) |
| **Money** | **Statements** (this month so far, then one a month, Download PDF), **Payouts** (what was paid and when), **Invoices** (fee invoices and Pay $...) |
| **Documents** | Agreements, forms, Forms C and D |
| **Account** | **Profile** (contact details, password), **Banking** (automatic debit, where we pay you), **Notifications** (our messages) |

### Top tasks

1. *Sign everything at once:* **Home** > **Check and sign**
2. *Set up the monthly debit:* **Account** > **Banking** > **Set up pre-authorized debit**
3. *Pay an invoice now:* **Money** > **Invoices**, the invoice, then **Pay $...**
4. *Payout details:* **Account** > **Banking** > **Where we pay you**
5. *Forms C and D:* **Documents** > **Sign Form C on screen** or **Sign Form D on screen**, with your witnesses beside you
6. *Book your own car:* **Cars** > **Bookings** > **Book my own car**
7. *New listing photos:* **Cars**, the car, then **Take new photos**
8. *Leave the program:* **Cars**, the car, then **Give notice**

### If something goes wrong

| What you see | What to do |
| --- | --- |
| **A link says it expired** | Links in our emails work for 24 hours, once. Press **Send me a new link** on that page. |
| **"Error 1102" on a page** | A short limit on our web host. Reload the page. You are still signed in. |
| **"That email and password do not match an account."** | Check the address, or use **Set a new password** on the sign-in page. |
| **A debit was returned** | You get an email with the reason. Insufficient funds: keep the money in the account for the retry, or pay the invoice from its page. Any other reason: pay from the invoice''s page or set up a new account under Account > Banking. |
