on Plan&quot;), or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out so the total is exactly that. The total shown is the total saved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Any length: past 30 days the monthly rate applies for each 30 days, and the monthly periods are listed. Each later period gets its own agreement, sent to the renter to sign a few days before it starts (Monthly periods on the booking; Send the agreement for the next period now if needed).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Choose how the rent is paid (e-Transfer or cash received, card on file, payment link, platform payout, insurer billed later; the ways open to you are set by an Admin; paid in parts: Add another payment) and then how the deposit is paid (card hold, cash or e-Transfer with its reference). Before you save sums it all up. The rental agreement is sent to the renter to sign online (never on paper). An insurance replacement with dates not known yet: untick Blocks the car&#39;s calendar and say why. Insurer billed later shows Charges to the insurer: type the rate a day of VLF, LDW, T&amp;LDW, PAP/PEC or Waiver Saver that the insurer authorized (empty: none); each is the rate times the days, plus HST, billed to the insurer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Under Who found this client, choose <b class="gd-ui">I sourced this client</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Entered for CarmaCars</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the rental</b>. The renter gets the confirmation email unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Do not email the renter</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div class="gd-t">A rental you add is credited to you and shows in My sales as a rental you added. If you sourced it, its commission shows there too.</div></li></ol></div><aside 